Cactus Code Thorn PlanesX
Author(s)    : Michail Chabanov
Maintainer(s): Michail Chabanov
Licence      : LGPL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Purpose

Output axis-aligned 2D slabs (xy / xz / yz planes) of CarpetX grid functions
at chosen world-coordinate elevations, in Silo and openPMD format. The output
is file-per-plane and AMR-aware (per-level snapping, Silo mrgtree level
shadowing, openPMD AMR-hierarchy attributes); Cartesian patches only.

PlanesX registers an IO method (CCTK_RegisterIOMethod) that CarpetX's
OutputGH calls after its built-in writers -- after the CCTK_ANALYSIS
traversal, so analysis-bin grid functions are output up to date. This
requires the CarpetX commit "call registered IO methods from OutputGH".
PlanesX follows CarpetX's output conventions (IO::out_dir,
out_mode/out_proc_every, openpmd_format, compression, cadence fallback to
CarpetX::out_{silo,openpmd}_every).

See doc/plane_output.md for parameters, file layout, the VisIt path, and the
TestPlanesX-based verification.
